WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:04.420
When was the last time you watched an anime that really had an effect on you?

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:07.960
No, I'm not talking about the last anime you enjoyed

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:12.600
The last time you had a cute waifu or husbando you cheerfully followed along with.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:15.240
The last time you laughed or cried during a show.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:19.980
I'm talking about the one that really made you rethink something in your actual life.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:27.400
One whose area of effect extended beyond the confines of the screen you are watching it on.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:33.460
That's. . embedded itself deep into your psyche long after you had finished watching it.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:37.120
It's a bittersweet feeling whenever you get it because

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:41.200
as you grow older, that feeling becomes increasingly harder to find.

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:45.600
Mostly because the older you get the more you learn about yourself and the world around you

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:50.480
that it becomes rarer for you to find something that really makes you reflect

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:53.420
on an aspect of yourself in a different light.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:58.760
So, today, I wanted to share my experiences around the latest show that managed

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:01.740
to have this effect on me and...

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:03.300
That was with

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.660
"A Place Further than the Universe."

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:09.740
now if you've kept up with the anime seasons or even just my Twitter,

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:12.320
you probably already know about this show

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:17.220
as it's made its rounds on the community as the "New critically acclaimed show of last season."

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:21.520
But you know past all the hype and the praise of its writing and

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:26.000
direction and technical aspects that people normally talk about.

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:29.080
For me it was one of the most

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:33.740
inspirational anime I've ever had the pleasure of viewing.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:39.360
It's been a long time since I've seen the show that's affected an audience on such an intimate level

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:43.500
And I was definitely one of them and all it is is about

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:47.300
a group of normal high school girls that journey to Antarctica,

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:52.260
[Chuckle] which many people have already happily pointed out

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:54.680
that is still very much within this universe.

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:58.000
Here's a little tangent about myself as a person.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:04.300
As a kid, I was a daydreamer. I'd spend so much of my time in my own head that people thought I was this

00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:08.914
really quiet uninteresting Asian kid that didn't have too many friends

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:12.360
because in my head I daydreamed about going on these grand

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:16.319
adventures and doing something exciting one day [Chuckle] even though

00:02:16.319 --> 00:02:19.949
I was just a lazy nerd who rarely got out of his room.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:26.280
But I think that was why I was so drawn to the escapism in anime and why I was so intimately drawn to this show

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:32.900
right from episode 1 when we are introduced to one of the girls who wakes up one day and

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:35.120
realizes that she feels...

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:41.860
like she's wasting her youth. She hasn't done all the crazy things she wanted to do and

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:47.980
cliche as this may be, I'm sure it's a feeling everyone's had at least one time in their lives.

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:53.700
You have these plans, you have these ambitions that you tell yourself you'll eventually get to

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:54.900
someday. . .

00:02:55.599 --> 00:02:56.300
. . . Someday. . .

00:02:56.740 --> 00:02:59.220
. . . But not today.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:03.920
Today you have school, or today you have a job, or you're just not feeling up for it,

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:06.660
or you have commitments, or it's just not the right time

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:10.880
then days past, weeks, months, then eventually years and

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:14.080
That someday never becomes...

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:15.520
today.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:20.200
A lot of the times we are just waiting for that one thing to push us over the edge

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.439
and many of us never stop waiting.

00:03:22.599 --> 00:03:27.100
But in the show's case she meets someone who couldn't be more different from her.

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:30.700
Someone who had the craziness and eccentricities she didn't,

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:35.820
who was not going to let anything or anyone get in the way of achieving her own ambitions,

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:38.260
which was to go to Antarctica.

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:41.180
That was her push, that was her signal

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:46.700
and seeing her take that first fearful step towards the journey she always wanted hit me

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:49.840
So much harder than I thought it would and

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:54.400
plastered this smile on my face that wouldn't be removed throughout the whole show.

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:58.880
I remember thinking "Man, if they get to Antarctica in Episode 3 and

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:03.810
this turns out to be a moe show about a bunch of cute girls dicking around with penguins,

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:07.100
I'm going to be SO disappointed."

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:10.800
But luckily it only expanded on moments like this

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:14.820
on the journey that they undertake and the bonds that they make.

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:19.360
It's so energetically captured that spirit of youth and adventure,

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:20.580
seizing the day and

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:23.069
all that cheesy inspirational crap you've heard before,

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:27.660
but portraying it in a way that feels so close to home.

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:31.649
Not as a quest with stakes bigger than people involved but as a

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:36.340
personal journey one shared with the friends you hold most dear with

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:38.580
a destination that was as

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:41.960
breathtaking as the journey that took us there.

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:44.000
There's this scene in Episode 7 I think,

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:47.640
where the girls are on this ship to their destination,

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:49.100
and it's the first time they've travelled by sea,

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:53.020
so of course it's the first time they've experienced sea-sickness

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:56.380
and it's just an absolutely awful time.

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:58.440
They can't sleep, they can't eat,

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:03.680
they're constantly feeling like complete crap and yet it turns into this little..

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:05.500
bonding experience for the group.

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:08.200
Like the girls just start laughing because

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:11.100
they're having an absolutely awful time

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:14.000
but they're having an awful time together

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:17.700
and that's what doesn't make it so bad.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:19.300
I love this scene.

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:23.698
Anyone who's been on a trip with friends knows that nothing goes exactly to plan.

00:05:23.949 --> 00:05:25.800
Something always goes wrong

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:28.499
and you may end up experiencing new things that you're...

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:33.300
you're not [x2] too fond of but, It's sharing this experience,

00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:35.860
this journey through its ups and downs

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:37.900
with the people you care about that

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:40.109
really secures the bonds you have with them.

00:05:40.109 --> 00:05:43.300
It's those moments that you'll look back on together in years time

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:47.180
and laugh at that as a tender memory even if at the time you

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:51.220
absolutely hated it and that's kind of the beauty of this show

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:54.120
that it manages to hit on such a...

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:56.120
A human level.

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:58.640
It isn't an incredibly deep show,

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:03.020
but it is a tender reminder of aspects many of us can find in ourselves.

00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:07.080
Whether it'd be the feeling like you're wasting your youth that

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:10.289
you need to do something to come to terms with an event in your life,

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:15.280
putting on a brave face even though all you want to do is kick and scream on the inside,

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:18.960
or never finding the friends who really cared about you.

00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:22.920
Watching these characters grow over the course of their journey

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:26.820
and fill in these aspects that they were missing in their lives has this

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:31.740
incredible power to ignite this desire to fill in some of the gaps in your own life.

00:06:31.980 --> 00:06:38.980
And that to me was way more powerful than the seas of motivational posters, quotes and speeches

00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:41.680
I've seen floating around on the Internet,

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:43.460
but I guess that's just it.

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:48.080
We've become desensitized to a lot of the things we see through a screen.

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:51.500
Reality shows commercialize their relatable sob story.

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:54.300
News turn tragedies into compelling narratives

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:58.340
Social media has put a glossy filter over everyone's lives

00:06:58.340 --> 00:07:01.680
that it's hard to distinguish what's real anymore.

00:07:01.700 --> 00:07:05.740
It's so easy to become cynical with the amount of bullshit

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:08.640
we are exposed to in this ever more connected world.

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:12.340
But maybe that's why something as innocently

00:07:12.340 --> 00:07:15.560
fake as four cute anime girls felt way more real

00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:19.180
and was able to blindside the cynical voice in the back of my head

00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:23.400
that tells me not to get swayed over something like this.

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:24.480
When the show ended,

00:07:24.490 --> 00:07:27.760
I was greeted with a bittersweet void I hadn't felt in so long.

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:30.160
I didn't want to watch any other anime

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:33.429
I didn't want to immediately log online and share my opinion.

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:38.470
I just wanted to let it sink in and truly reflect on the experience it had given me and...

00:07:38.660 --> 00:07:40.940
When I realized that, I just thought

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:43.400
How long has it been since I've felt this feeling?

00:07:43.540 --> 00:07:46.780
How long has it been since I truly cherished what a show could do

00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:49.000
and really let it run its course

00:07:49.220 --> 00:07:52.300
And that brings me to what I was saying at the beginning

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:58.960
every so often you find that anime, or that movie, or that song that has a profound effect on your life and

00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:03.860
makes you think deeper about yourself, and it really sticks with you for a while

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:08.180
That feeling is becoming harder and harder to find in this day and age,

00:08:08.180 --> 00:08:09.399
not just because you get older

00:08:09.470 --> 00:08:11.980
But because we consume so much media now

00:08:11.980 --> 00:08:14.460
that new things are constantly pushed in our face

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:15.669
that we don't even have time to reflect

00:08:15.669 --> 00:08:19.120
on the last thing we watched to let it sink in

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:21.880
and I don't know if I'm being old-fashioned in feeling like...

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:25.780
When you always have something to move on to immediately.

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:30.600
You forget to hold on to the things that you find truly special and

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:33.740
I think it's something we're slowly losing

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:36.500
in this modern world of abundancy.

00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:40.620
So I decided to do something stupid

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:44.380
I decided to let myself BE inspired by this innocent show.

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:46.190
Go on a journey to a place

00:08:46.190 --> 00:08:47.640
I've never been before

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:49.960
and do things I had never done

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:52.660
without any pressure to keep up with anime or the internet.

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:55.320
Because I wanted to remember.

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:59.000
Remember why anime had such a big effect on me when I was younger.

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:04.100
Remember the craziness I felt when I abandoned my career to pursue this medium as a job.

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:06.480
Remember that it shook me more than

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:09.760
just a commodity we watched discussed and forget and

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:14.100
cement myself that just because I felt inspired by a fictional

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:18.760
constructed story of four cute girls doing something amazing with their lives.

00:09:18.860 --> 00:09:23.220
It doesn't mean the experience was any less real for me.

00:09:23.300 --> 00:09:24.660
Because it wasn't.

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:30.080
[Music]

00:09:30.180 --> 00:09:32.820
That's really what I wanted to get off my chest.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:36.320
I'm not sure if I was trying to say anything aside from,

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:39.880
"Hey I think this is a pretty good show and you should give it a shot."

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:43.890
But for me it reminded me a few things I might have known

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:47.760
but have forgotten over the years. It reminded me that I

00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:50.740
value looking at the world through an optimistic lens.

00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:52.890
It reminded me to value the bonds

00:09:52.890 --> 00:09:55.469
I've made with the friends that I have and

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:59.160
as someone who did do something as reckless with their life

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:00.210
as quitting their career

00:10:00.210 --> 00:10:03.179
that had sunk years of their life into for an Internet job

00:10:03.180 --> 00:10:08.250
It was my personal reminder that I could turn that someday...

00:10:09.160 --> 00:10:10.600
into today.

00:10:12.100 --> 00:10:17.800
The End

